# Atlas Platform

Atlas is the **company operating system**. See `atlas-operating-system.mdc`.
It is **not** a medical device. Tenant products in Atlas may be.

## Clinical data

FHIR R4 is the internal and external model for clinical data. Experiences
(Zone 2) call the FHIR API only. Every query filters by `organization_id`.

## Trust zones

Zone 1 Auth Proxy → Zone 2 Experiences → Zone 3 Platform → Zone 4 Data →
Zone 5 AI → Zone 6 Integration.

Zone 2 never touches the database or AI directly. Zone 3 is the only zone
that talks to Zone 4 and Zone 5.

## Design controls

The Atlas Design Controls MCP is the sole store. See `mcp-sole-source.mdc`.
The product ID comes from the **home-repo overlay**. Do not guess it.

## ID patterns (Atlas platform product)

User Need `UN-ATLAS-XXX` · Design Input `DI-ATLAS-XXX` · Design Output
`DO-ATLAS-XXX-YYY` · Verification `VT-ATLAS-XXX` · Validation
`VAL-ATLAS-XXX` · Risk `R-ATLAS-XXX`. Tenant products may use hex dcIds.
Do not invent IDs that collide with retired ones.

## Non-negotiables

- Know the safety class (A / B / C) before writing code.
- Audit every data access and change. Audit is append-only.
- AI outputs must show confidence, allow override, and create Provenance.
- New work follows this pack. Secrets from Key Vault only.
